TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Confirmed that checkpoint cp-smoke failed against a witnessed base that predates the authorized fix, so attempt 2 would re-run the identical broken probe. Evidence: (1) the task workspace pins baseRev=1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304 and the diff is empty (head == baseRev), so nothing in the lane can change what ran; (2) `git merge-base --is-ancestor 7509202 HEAD` reports NOT-ANCESTOR — the two commits that overseer steering comment 6 declares as the fix, 9480958 (\"checkpoint purity: restore receipts unchanged modulo ts on re-run\", adding scripts/receipt-restore.py) and 7509202 (\"cp-smoke: admission probe matches patches/0008's boolean predicate\"), sit on main directly *above* 1e2eef7 and are absent from the checkpoint's base; (3) scripts/run-smoke.sh at the witnessed base still contains the defective line `ok, why = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym)`, while patches/0008 (see patches/MANIFEST.md and the pinned tests at patches/0008-ROCm-Enable-block-FP8-fused-MoE-on-gfx1151-via-in-ke.patch:126, which assert the bare call) defines that hook as a plain boolean predicate — the two-tuple unpack raises TypeError inside `try_(\"admission\", admission)`, sets the receipt status to fail, quarantines it under results/receipts/failed/, and the trailing verifier exits 1. That is exactly the failure the steward already isolated (inbox receipt 41) and exactly what 7509202 repairs; the repair is simply not in the base this attempt executed. The captured stdout (\"smoke receipt: .../results/receipts/smoke.json (fail receipts land under results/receipts/failed/)\") with exitCode 1 and empty stderr is consistent with the container probe running, the admission probe failing, and no pass receipt being produced. Why blocked rather than retry: cp-smoke is a checkpoint whose argv is fixed by the worklist and whose brief forbids repository modification, so no action inside this task's authority can pull commits 9480958 and 7509202 into its base; the correction is a task-set/base re-pin outside the lane. Not transient: the run is deterministic and reproducible, with no machinery or session fault in evidence.","proposal":{"kind":"gate-set-fix","paths":["scripts/run-smoke.sh","scripts/receipt-restore.py"],"goal":"Re-cut the cp-smoke checkpoint against a witnessed base that contains the already-landed fixes rather than the stale base 1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304. Advance the cp-smoke task revision so its workspace baseRev is main HEAD 75092021daf062687535b6cae2d47c02c65359f0, which includes 9480958 (scripts/receipt-restore.py plus its invocation from the cp-* entry scripts, satisfying the checkpoint-purity contract) and 7509202 (the admission probe calling TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme bare and recording reason \"boolean predicate (patches/0008)\"). The command must stay bash scripts/run-smoke.sh; only the base the checkpoint validates changes. With that base, all five probes (arch, fp8_cast, registry, aperture, admission) are expected to pass and a pass receipt should land at results/receipts/smoke.json, leaving tracked files byte-identical on a second re-run.","acceptance":[{"id":"base-contains-fixes","description":"The cp-smoke workspace base contains both fix commits, so the executed script is the corrected one.","argv":["bash","-c","git merge-base --is-ancestor 9480958 HEAD && git merge-base --is-ancestor 7509202 HEAD && ! grep -q 'ok, why = TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme' scripts/run-smoke.sh && test -f scripts/receipt-restore.py"]},{"id":"smoke-passes","description":"The fixed checkpoint command exits 0 and writes a pass receipt with all five probes green.","argv":["bash","scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},{"id":"smoke-idempotent","description":"Re-running the checkpoint over the already-correct base leaves every tracked file byte-identical, satisfying the checkpoint-purity contract.","argv":["bash","-c","bash scripts/run-smoke.sh && test -z \"$(git status --porcelain -- results scripts)\""]}],"dependencies":["cp-build"]}}
